===Etymology===
From {{etyl|grc|en}} {{m|grc|Πύθων|}}, the name of the mythological enormous serpent at Delphi slain by Apollo, from {{m|grc|Πῡθώ}}, the early name of Delphi, from {{m|grc|πυθώ||to rot, to decay}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/ˈpaɪθən/|lang=en}}
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|/ˈpaɪθɑːn/|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A type of large [[constrict]]ing [[snake]].
# {{lb|en|vulgar|slang}} [[penis]]

